---
source: tests/output.rs
expression: run.stdout()
---
ok      .vault/data holds 3 sealed entries
ok      .vault/keys is present
ok      .vault/recipients lists 1 recipient
ok      this clone is unlocked
ok      filter.vault.clean is configured
ok      filter.vault.smudge is configured
problem filter.vault.required is not true, so a failing filter would let git store the raw bytes
ok      filter.vault-plaintext.clean refuses plaintext secrets
ok      filter.vault-plaintext.required is true
warning core.fsmonitor is unset, so nothing seals a secret edit until the next commit attempt, which then reports that it left the edit out
problem diff.vault.cachetextconv is not false, so decrypted secrets would be cached under .git and outlive `git vault lock`
ok      the pre-commit hook is installed
ok      .vault/data is tracked normally
ok      .gitattributes hands .vault/data to the filters
problem `secrets/**` is sealed but not in .gitignore, so git may commit its plaintext
problem `secrets/leaky.env` is sealed and also tracked in plaintext. Run `git vault add secrets/leaky.env`
